    "result_text": "Those are only the `LuhnCheckDigit` utility (still used) \u2014 no references to the removed fields remain. The implementation is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit` field.\n\n**New/renamed logic (single-responsibility units):**\n- **`MemberIdGenerator`** (replaces `CustomerCodeGenerator` + `MembershipNumberGenerator`) \u2014 builds the id from REGION, the 2-digit fiscal year (via the existing `FiscalYear`), the 8-upper-hex `HASH8` (the same `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)` first-8-hex as the region-and-hash identity), and a single Luhn `CHK` over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>` (reusing `LuhnCheckDigit`). Its `regionOf` parses REGION as the leading non-digit run, which also stays correct across any `-<n>` dedup suffix.\n- **`MemberIdDeduplicator`** (replaces `CustomerCodeDeduplicator`) \u2014 collision handling now applies to the `memberId`.\n\n**Wiring updated to reference the memberId:**\n- `Owner` \u2014 replaced the `customer_code`/`membership_number` columns and their accessors with a single `member_id`; removed `getCheckDigit()`; `getPrimaryIdentifier()` and `getLocality()` (which drives `getOwnerSegment`) now read the member id.\n- `OwnerRestControllerV1.createOwner` \u2014 generates and de-duplicates the member id in one step before persisting.\n- `OwnerAuditLogger` / `OwnerCreatedEvent` \u2014 the audit line and structured event now carry `memberId`.\n- Deleted the three obsolete classes and fixed a stale javadoc link in `CityOwnerCounter`.\n\n**Contract & schema:**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 replaced the `customerCode`, `membershipNumber` and `checkDigit` properties with a single `memberId`, and updated the `locality` description. (DTOs are generated from this spec at build time.)\n- All four DB schemas (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres) \u2014 swapped `customer_code` + `membership_number` for `member_id`.\n\n`./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. Sample audit output confirms the format: `memberId=NSW2716E6609E1` (NSW \u00b7 FY27 \u00b7 HASH8 `16E6609E` \u00b7 CHK `1`).",
